well we're at one of uh three cordons in  liverpool tonight in what is a major  incident  led by the northwest counter terrorism  unit it happened just before  the minute silence was held across the  country  and  from what we know  we think it was a taxi pulled up to the  liverpool women's hospital  and then there was  some sort of explosion  the car  was destroyed by fire one man we know  died in that fire another man the dry he  was a passenger the driver got out of  that vehicle  and was injured had to be taken to  hospital the area was obviously  sealed off  and then shortly afterwards this cordon  and another one was set up meanwhile um  a brief news conference was held  by the chief constable  and that told us something about how  seriously this was being taken here is  what she had to say  so far we understand that the car  involved was a taxi which pulled up at  the hospital shortly before the  explosion occurred  work is still ongoing to establish what  has happened and could  take some time before we in a position  to confirm anything  we are keeping an open mind as to what  caused the explosion but given how it  has happened and out of caution  counter-terrorism police are leading the  investigation supported by merseyside  police  and it wasn't long uh after that  explosion before armed police swooped  here at rutland avenue just a mile away  from the hospital and also at bowler  street in kensington  here residents have been told they are  not allowed to leave their homes they've  been told this cordon at least if they  do leave they won't be allowed to come  back and this cordon they've been told  could be in place for some time  and in the kensington area the police  have confirmed three men have been  arrested in connection with this  incident under the terrorism act aged 21  26 and 29  but it is important to point out that  the terror unit says that it is keeping  an open mind still  about what was behind this explosion and  they are working with merseyside police
 

